# PCoA with Overlaid Ellipses for Lc, Gv, and LcGv

This R script performs ordination analysis on a metabolite intensity matrix and produces a PCoA scatter plot with overlaid confidence ellipses. It preprocesses the data with zero replacement, log2 transformation, and Pareto scaling (column-wise), then computes a Manhattan distance matrix and runs classical multidimensional scaling (`cmdscale`) to obtain PCo1/PCo2 coordinates.

Points are colored by sample group, shaped by biological replicate (1, 2, 3), and three 90% confidence ellipses are overlaid: one around all Lc-containing groups, one around all Gv-containing groups, and one around the specific LcGv group.

## Input

- `VaBaMet_matrix.csv` with a `short name` column for metabolite labels and intensity columns named `<replicate>.<group>` (e.g., `1.LcGv`, `2.Gv`).

## Output

- `VaBaMet_PCoA_manhattan.png` (6×6 in, 300 dpi)
- `VaBaMet_PCoA_manhattan.svg`

## Requirements

R with `ggplot2` and `svglite`.

## Note

The group color palette is hardcoded for 15 named groups — update `group_colors` if your labels differ. Variance percentages are shown on the axis labels from the PCoA eigenvalues.
